          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nPerfect! The implementation is complete. Let me create a final summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI have successfully implemented the `ST_S2ToGeom` public API across the Apache Sedona codebase. Here's what was delivered:\n\n### Core Implementation\n\n1. **Common Java Module** (`/workspace/common/src/main/java/org/apache/sedona/common/Functions.java`)\n   - Added `s2ToGeom(long[] cells)` - converts S2 cell IDs to MultiPolygon geometry\n   - Added `s2ToGeom(Long[] cells)` - overloaded method for boxed arrays\n   - Preserves cell ID order in output\n   - Returns MULTIPOLYGON compatible with ST_Collect\n\n2. **Spark SQL** \n   - Expression class in `Functions.scala`\n   - Registered in `Catalog.scala`\n   - DataFrame API in `st_functions.scala` with Column and Array[Long] overloads\n\n3. **Flink SQL**\n   - Scalar function class in `Functions.java`\n   - Registered in `Catalog.java`\n\n4. **Python DataFrame API**\n   - Added to `st_functions.py` with proper type hints\n   - Supports both column and list inputs\n\n### Key Features\n\n✅ **Order Preservation**: Output maintains original cell ID order  \n✅ **Intersection Guarantee**: Each polygon intersects source geometry  \n✅ **ST_Collect Compatible**: Produces MULTIPOLYGON when aggregated  \n✅ **Multiple Input Formats**: Supports primitive arrays, boxed arrays, columns, and lists  \n✅ **Spatial Operations Ready**: Returns Geometry objects for ST_Intersects and other operations  \n\n### Tests\n\n- Spark Scala tests in `STS2ToGeom.scala`\n- DataFrame API tests in `dataFrameAPITestScala.scala`\n- Flink Java tests in `FunctionTest.java`\n- Python tests in `test_function.py`\n\nThe implementation follows the same pattern as the existing `ST_H3ToGeom` function and is fully integrated into the Sedona ecosystem.",
